@ThunderBandit are you basing that on Mat’s lame and totally untrue demonstration of the technique that he claimed to find by Googling? That is totally false. I’d be amazed if any Tesla owners have ever used that bizarre technique.

The handle has a thicker section for the thumb. As you press your thumb on that section, the longer section extends into your palm so you pull the handle with one continuous motion. It can easily be done in a split second as Mat demonstrates several times using the correct technique when he’s making his second false claim about the doors not closing properly. This happens immediately after his rant about not knowing how to open the doors! He uses the long section of the handle after he’s just asked what the long section of the handle is for? It’s so obviously staged.

To count that as a two-step process would be the equivalent of saying that the BYD technique of wrapping your hand around the handle and then pulling is a two-step process!
